# 💧 Smart Water Tank Controller Using Arduino UNO

An embedded systems project that automatically monitors water level and environmental conditions while simulating automatic pump control.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project uses an Arduino UNO to monitor the water level inside a storage tank using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor. It also measures ambient temperature and humidity using a DHT11 sensor.

Based on the measured water level, the system automatically controls a relay (representing a water pump), provides visual and audible alerts, and displays real-time information on both a 16×2 LCD and a 0.96" OLED display.

This project demonstrates practical applications of Embedded Systems, Sensor Integration, and IoT-ready automation.

---

## Features

- Water level measurement
- Water level percentage calculation
- Automatic pump control using relay
- Temperature monitoring
- Humidity monitoring
- OLED dashboard
- LCD status display
- Low water alarm using buzzer
- LED status indicator
- Real-time sensor monitoring

